        <item>
            <title>0.6.7</title>
            <pubDate>Thu, 05 Nov 2026 17:43:25 -0500</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>55</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.6.7</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<h2>Assembly 0.6.7</h2>
<p>Aligning lavs to the boom:</p>
<ul>
  <li><b>Align Selected Clips no longer refuses clips that start one sample
    before a frame.</b> Assembled clips often start there, and they were being
    left alone with the reason "no exact start in its roll".</li>
  <li><b>A report track for alignments.</b> A track named like
    <b>ALN Report</b> marks each place worth looking at:
    <ul>
      <li><b>NOT ALIGNED:</b> refused before any audio was read.</li>
      <li><b>LEFT ALONE:</b> read, and deliberately not changed.</li>
      <li><b>FAILED:</b> could not be rendered.</li>
      <li><b>CHECK:</b> aligned, but listen here first.</li>
      <li>Each take gets one entry saying how many clips and why, and
        <b>Save Diagnostic Report…</b> lists every clip behind it.</li>
      <li>Turn it off with <b>Report</b> in the Align sheet.</li>
    </ul></li>
  <li><b>When nothing can be aligned, an alert says why,</b> where before
    there was only a line in the status bar.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
